 "boundary": [
  "DO NOT read the write counts as 'how many writers exist': 24 of updateNeedsToBeSent's 29 sites are labelled pointer-or-unknown because the classifier only inspects the instruction after the address computation, and these sites use strb rX,[rY,rZ] store forms it does not recognise. '0 writers' would be a wrong conclusion drawn from a classifier gap.",
  "the flag getters sit in a run of adjacent functions (0x83d1xx), so prologue attribution packs several of their self-reads under DynamicObject -[uniqueID]; cell identity is reliable, method naming is not, exactly as recorded for the shared one-line getters.",
  "the reads being coherent is an observation, not proof that every labelled site is a flag use."
 ]
